{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift","id":962769,"title":"A question regarding a certain gift.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-03T04:48:05-07:00","id":962769,"title":"A question regarding a certain gift.","content":"So there's this gift, called &quot;Paws of the newborn cub&quot;, I was wondering if there's some sort of a counter-measure against that?<br /> A way to somehow cancel the gift perhaps? <br /> Anything at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T06:01:53-07:00","id":962785,"title":"","content":"It's a level 5 gift that requires a roll to use and only lasts a few turns. Why should it have a counter measure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T06:14:32-07:00","id":962787,"title":"","content":"Double-checked the book just to be sure, and no... I don't see and can't really think of a countermeasure to this. Keep in mind, it's a Rank 5 Silver Fang gift... so there are seriously only a small handful of beings on the planet that can use it. There's a reason the Silver Fangs are the leaders of the Garou, and a reason that any Garou that somehow lives long enough and survives enough battles to be a Grand Elder is a rightfully terrifying opponent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T07:24:20-07:00","id":962815,"title":"","content":"Agreeing with the responses above.<br /> <br /> I'm also curious why this question came up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T07:28:05-07:00","id":962817,"title":"","content":"I second that curiosity.<br /> <br /> Also... here's a question that I don't know if the books every really addressed- What about the Spirit sphere for Mages? I don't know if it would be able to counter a relatively instant gift whose literal and immediate effect is taking away someone's powers (especially if the Mage in question doesn't know about the Gift or that it's about to be used on them)... but what about Spirit vs. Gifts and Spirit Charms in general?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T07:45:25-07:00","id":962822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962817#post962817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also... here's a question that I don't know if the books every really addressed- What about the Spirit sphere for Mages? I don't know if it would be able to counter a relatively instant gift whose literal and immediate effect is taking away someone's powers (especially if the Mage in question doesn't know about the Gift or that it's about to be used on them)... but what about Spirit vs. Gifts and Spirit Charms in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how much of a crossover game you're playing?<br /> Here is my understanding of it (heavily influenced by a similar discussion recently in the Mage forums where I was asking about countermagic):<br /> Running Mages just from the Werewolf book, they don't get automatic countermagic so the gift works just fine.<br /> Running Mages from a Mage book, they can attempt countermagic reflexively against powers that specifically target them, assuming they have the right Spheres (seems like it in this example). I don't believe they need foreknowledge of the power to do so.<br /> <br /> The Spirit Sphere can usually be used to counter Gifts and Spirit Charms in general. However, normal countermagic takes away successes, so if a power doesn't require a roll, like some gifts and charms, then the Mage needs to actually use an action to counter it and so instant effects may very well get passed them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:45:03-07:00","id":962855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962815#post962815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreeing with the responses above.<br /> <br /> I'm also curious why this question came up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm RP'ing a mage, and I've come across a certain sept of werewolves whom I had to take care of since I was being attacked ,which I did, but then this elder arrived and rendered me completely helpless with this gift lmao, and since usually there's a counter measure for almost everything I was pretty sure there would be something for this as well. (For an example there're herbs that shield you mentally by increasing the attacker's difficulty to influence you, etc)<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962822#post962822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how much of a crossover game you're playing?<br /> Here is my understanding of it (heavily influenced by a similar discussion recently in the Mage forums where I was asking about countermagic):<br /> Running Mages just from the Werewolf book, they don't get automatic countermagic so the gift works just fine.<br /> Running Mages from a Mage book, they can attempt countermagic reflexively against powers that specifically target them, assuming they have the right Spheres (seems like it in this example). I don't believe they need foreknowledge of the power to do so.<br /> <br /> The Spirit Sphere can usually be used to counter Gifts and Spirit Charms in general. However, normal countermagic takes away successes, so if a power doesn't require a roll, like some gifts and charms, then the Mage needs to actually use an action to counter it and so instant effects may very well get passed them.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So if my mage has the spirit sphere I can countermagic fera gifts?<br /> To use this gift the wolf had to use two gnosis points if I'm not mistaken, then he rolled his perm gnosis rate with my willpower as a difficulty; each success is a turn in which I'm completely stripped off my magic.<br /> <br /> Eitherway I was just assuming that there should be something that would help me going up against that. I suppose the only way is to stay away from this wolf, or perhaps attack via Correspondence while maintaining distance. After all from what I've understood if he doesn't see me he can't just use that gift on me, correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","user":"MowtekPvP","date":". 09-03-2016, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:54:48-07:00","id":962858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962855#post962855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm RP'ing a mage, and I've come across a certain sept of werewolves whom I had to take care of since I was being attacked ,which I did, but then this elder arrived and rendered me completely helpless with this gift lmao, and since usually there's a counter measure for almost everything I was pretty sure there would be something for this as well. (For an example there're herbs that shield you mentally by increasing the attacker's difficulty to influence you, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming &quot;take care of&quot; means fought and/or killed? I'm not sure how you took on a Sept of Werewolves.<br /> That is pretty much exactly what the Gift does. It's Rank 5. One of the most powerful Gifts a Garou can have access to. With most player stats, you <i>should</i> get steamrolled by Elders.<br /> What herbs give you mental power defense? That shouldn't be a thing unless the herbs are just a focus for your magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962855#post962855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if my mage has the spirit sphere I can countermagic fera gifts?<br /> To use this gift the wolf had to use two gnosis points if I'm not mistaken, then he rolled his perm gnosis rate with my willpower as a difficulty; each success is a turn in which I'm completely stripped off my magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like the system for the Gift. And yea, it completely strips a being of all supernatural powers, for just a few turns. This includes innate powers like shapeshifting and blood buffing. Mages as rendered completely normally mortal.<br /> <br /> What edition are you playing? I believe that makes a difference in how countermagic works.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:57:49-07:00","id":962862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962855#post962855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all from what I've understood if he doesn't see me he can't just use that gift on me, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind also these are werewolves, they don't need to &quot;see&quot; you to know you are there. They have smell, hearing, and W20 gave the skill primal urge a pretty big boost (lets you search for magically hidden enemies with a diff 8 roll).<br /> <br /> My big suggestion is build up the will power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 09-03-2016, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:02:25-07:00","id":962865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962858#post962858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming &quot;take care of&quot; means fought and/or killed? I'm not sure how you took on a Sept of Werewolves.<br /> That is pretty much exactly what the Gift does. It's Rank 5. One of the most powerful Gifts a Garou can have access to. With most player stats, you <i>should</i> get steamrolled by Elders.<br /> What herbs give you mental power defense? That shouldn't be a thing unless the herbs are just a focus for your magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That sounds like the system for the Gift. And yea, it completely strips a being of all supernatural powers, for just a few turns. This includes innate powers like shapeshifting and blood buffing. Mages as rendered completely normally mortal.<br /> <br /> What edition are you playing? I believe that makes a difference in how countermagic works.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Playing the 20th anniv' edition<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962862#post962862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind also these are werewolves, they don't need to &quot;see&quot; you to know you are there. They have smell, hearing, and W20 gave the skill primal urge a pretty big boost (lets you search for magically hidden enemies with a diff 8 roll).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that would work if I'm scrying them with correspondence, would it? I mean there is nothing to smell or hear, since I could be anywhere in the world with enough successes, watching them from a-far.<br /> Not sure if Primal Urge would work though? would it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:04:41-07:00","id":962868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962865#post962865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that would work if I'm scrying them with correspondence, would it? I mean there is nothing to smell or hear, since I could be anywhere in the world with enough successes, watching them from a-far.<br /> Not sure if Primal Urge would work though? would it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You got Paws of the Newborn Cub used on you and you survived the fight and were able to flee?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:06:55-07:00","id":962869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962865#post962865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing the 20th anniv' edition<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think that would work if I'm scrying them with correspondence, would it? I mean there is nothing to smell or hear, since I could be anywhere in the world with enough successes, watching them from a-far.<br /> Not sure if Primal Urge would work though? would it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think primal urge would work there, as you're not actually there. I think I misunderstood what your plans were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:10:06-07:00","id":962870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962868#post962868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You got Paws of the Newborn Cub used on you and you survived the fight and were able to flee?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm RP'ing with a few friends of mine who are also RP'ing mages, so I was teleported out of harm just in time. Of course I tried to talk myself out of that at first but it was no use for obvious reasons :3<br /> Anyway, just barely managed to get away, more luck than brains really.I just didn't expect an elder this strong, so ye.<br /> Also had this enchanted armor that kept me alive long enough for my buddies to help me out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962869#post962869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think primal urge would work there, as you're not actually there. I think I misunderstood what your plans were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good, guess I got my answer then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","user":"MowtekPvP","date":". 09-03-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:27:32-07:00","id":962878,"title":"","content":"Scrying onto a Cearn, especially one with Rank 5 elders in residence isn't (or shouldn't be) a thing.<br /> <br /> In any case, since you are playing Mage I expect that you'll continue to roll over Garou with little real resistance. That seems to be how most Mage games are described.<br /> <br /> How did you guys take on a Sept of Werewolves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:41:25-07:00","id":962882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962878#post962878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scrying onto a Cearn, especially one with Rank 5 elders in residence isn't (or shouldn't be) a thing.<br /> <br /> In any case, since you are playing Mage I expect that you'll continue to roll over Garou with little real resistance. That seems to be how most Mage games are described.<br /> <br /> How did you guys take on a Sept of Werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>We were about four magis, really just minding our own business. The wolves attacked us because we were in their turf, although we really weren't aware of that. One of the magis who were with me had Correspondence 4, life 4, spirit 4 and prime 4. he's pretty powerful, anyway what he did there is quite simple really, while I was getting all the attention (had to use some pretty vulgar magic to get their attention, used forces) he was working on a ward, somehow I and the other 2 managed to distract the wolves just enough time for him to bring up a ward with enough successes to make sure we will be able to avoid direct combat and simply teleport away afterwards. (He got really lucky with the rolls so somehow we managed to escape)<br /> he also had this periapt with him where he stored quite a bit of quintessence which helped him out quite a bit (it's a periapt righT? since im pretty new to this, not sure whether it's a periapt or something else, the one that stores quintessence i mean). And the elder could use that gift only on one of us at the time, so he used that on me. I took on quite a few attacks, but I had this armor that kept me alive just long enough for the others to get themselves and me out of there..<br /> <br /> <br /> I just didn't get one thing, he could just teleport us away lol idk wtf he was doing there honestly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","user":"MowtekPvP","date":". 09-03-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T11:17:37-07:00","id":962902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962882#post962882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just didn't get one thing, he could just teleport us away lol idk wtf he was doing there honestly</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire encounter sounds bizarre. A lot fo that just shouldn't go the way it did. In any case, you survived and left. Why bother planning on going back and confronting them again?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T11:26:29-07:00","id":962907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962902#post962902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire encounter sounds bizarre. A lot fo that just shouldn't go the way it did. In any case, you survived and left. Why bother planning on going back and confronting them again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're still after me apparently","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T13:32:31-07:00","id":962957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962907#post962907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they're still after me apparently</div> </div> </div> </div>oh. weird. well, sort of. What Spheres/Arete do you have?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T17:56:40-07:00","id":963020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962785#post962785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a level 5 gift that requires a roll to use and only lasts a few turns. Why should it have a counter measure?</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's no counter to the said gift, it's Rank 5 for a reason. Silver Fangs are the leaders of the Garou Nation and are known to be one of the greatest klaive-masters, confronting an elder of the Silver Fangs isn't something you should do, not to mention a whole sept of werewolves where elders are present -- the best you can do is stray away from their path and not bother with them. As previously mentioned, attempting to scry a caern is just asking for trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","user":"Darko","date":". 09-03-2016, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T19:28:40-07:00","id":963047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962957#post962957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh. weird. well, sort of. What Spheres/Arete do you have?</div> </div> </div> </div>5 arete. Forces 4, Corresp 4, Life 3, Prime 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T20:23:31-07:00","id":963073,"title":"","content":"So yea, if you insist on fighting them, Corr/Forces is your best bet.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, with that much Corr, you should be able to avoid them. There is no reason they should be able to find you if you're careful. And the easiest fight is the one you avoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T04:47:58-07:00","id":963628,"title":"","content":"Correspondence 4+Forces4+Prime 2=Raining fire (or your prefered Forces Attack) down on their Sept from your living room. Seriously, at those levels you can scan an enormous area for their lifesigns (with Life 3+Correspondence 2) and take them out either one by one or as a group. One big ritual (something like 10-20 successes on an extended Arete roll). No need at all to be anyway near them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T08:03:39-07:00","id":963693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=963628#post963628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correspondence 4+Forces4+Prime 2=Raining fire (or your prefered Forces Attack) down on their Sept from your living room. Seriously, at those levels you can scan an enormous area for their lifesigns (with Life 3+Correspondence 2) and take them out either one by one or as a group. One big ritual (something like 10-20 successes on an extended Arete roll). No need at all to be anyway near them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are various reasons that shouldn't work, but seeing how it's a Mage game I wouldn't be surprised if it did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T12:59:56-07:00","id":966874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=962882#post962882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just didn't get one thing, he could just teleport us away lol idk wtf he was doing there honestly</div> </div> </div> </div>And so can you...<br /> Correspondence 4<br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:24:09-07:00","id":966891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=963047#post963047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 arete. Forces 4, Corresp 4, Life 3, Prime 3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Firestorm in the hideout seems a fine solution to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> What kind of base do these werewolves have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-10-2016, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:27:08-07:00","id":966893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=966891#post966891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Firestorm in the hideout seems a fine solution to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Mages could do that into Garou Caerns, then there wouldn't be any Garou left. Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:33:02-07:00","id":966895,"title":"","content":"Why? Garou and mages are not at odds, or at least not too much, mages have no reason to kill garou, they need a good reason to engage them, and mostly conflict comes from nodes/caerns propriety rights.<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides,there is a reason if mages after all these centuries retains a lot of nodes, despite garou opposition.<br /> <br /> The consanguinity of eternal Joy even used a Black Spiral Dancer pit as node, and there wasn't much the spirals could do about it (not that anyone could do anything about what Paramaguru Voormas wants).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-10-2016, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:15:27-07:00","id":967038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=966895#post966895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Garou and mages are not at odds, or at least not too much, mages have no reason to kill garou, they need a good reason to engage them, and mostly conflict comes from nodes/caerns propriety rights.<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides,there is a reason if mages after all these centuries retains a lot of nodes, despite garou opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure metatext. They aren't the same game, and the games themselves often end up being written in dramatically different fashion depending on the writer. The Mage rules, however, have always been barely passable at best. Not much of a journey from 1e, when the system was flat out unusable and required the player's guide to function.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The consanguinity of eternal Joy even used a Black Spiral Dancer pit as node, and there wasn't much the spirals could do about it (not that anyone could do anything about what Paramaguru Voormas wants). </div> </div> </div>They were just lucky they did it there and not in the Trinity Hive. Zhyzhak would have smashed his skull into fragments - broken, pitiful, eternally undying fragments that could only cry out in agony. The Green Dragon agreed, don't bother him about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T03:02:45-07:00","id":967247,"title":"","content":"Zhyzhak cannot defeat Voormas.<br /> Voormas in terms of sheer power vastly outclass the average vampire methuselah.<br /> <br /> He has a ridiculous dice pool to hit and dodge (at least 16 dice), thanks to the Shivasakti avatar war form, more than 20 dices of effects prepared, and just to face him you must get three 6 on a willpower roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> With 20 (or more) success worth of additional effect already prepared he is a death machine.<br /> <br /> Let's say he has 5 effect's dice of entropy 2 effect to hit at -3 difficult, 5 effect's dice of correspondence 2 effect to raise to 9 the base difficult to hit him, and a 10 success success for a effect Time 4, Entropy 4 ,Life 3 entropic explosion that at the first time he's hitten hits the attacker in chest ( 4 base success, 6 successo to damage, for a total of 12 dice of agg damage).<br /> <br /> <br /> So Zhyzak needs a 9 to hit him, and if she hits him she dies, moreover he just needs a 3 to hit, and he has much more dices.<br /> Even more, matter 3 and he turns his weapons in silver.<br /> So, no, Voormas is a demi-godlike figure, is just one step belove an Oracle,and that means he is far above Zhyzak and every Fera.<br /> <br /> You'd need a big spirit to face him, Fenris' war avatar big, or Simoon big.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:14:32-07:00","id":967318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967247#post967247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zhyzhak cannot defeat Voormas.<br /> Voormas in terms of sheer power vastly outclass the average vampire methuselah.<br /> <br /> He has a ridiculous dice pool to hit and dodge (at least 16 dice), thanks to the Shivasakti avatar war form, more than 20 dices of effects prepared, and just to face him you must get three 6 on a willpower roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> With 20 (or more) success worth of additional effect already prepared he is a death machine.<br /> <br /> Let's say he has 5 effect's dice of entropy 2 effect to hit at -3 difficult, 5 effect's dice of correspondence 2 effect to raise to 9 the base difficult to hit him, and a 10 success success for a effect Time 4, Entropy 4 ,Life 3 entropic explosion that at the first time he's hitten hits the attacker in chest ( 4 base success, 6 successo to damage, for a total of 12 dice of agg damage).<br /> <br /> <br /> So Zhyzak needs a 9 to hit him, and if she hits him she dies, moreover he just needs a 3 to hit, and he has much more dices.<br /> Even more, matter 3 and he turns his weapons in silver.<br /> So, no, Voormas is a demi-godlike figure, is just one step belove an Oracle,and that means he is far above Zhyzak and every Fera.<br /> <br /> You'd need a big spirit to face him, Fenris' war avatar big, or Simoon big.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying your Mage icon should be defeated but there are some points above worth disputing.<br /> 1) As of M20, doesn't every supernatural creature with an occult rating get countermagic? Attacking a Caern/Pit then puts a serious cramp in the effects being thrown around.<br /> 2) It's not dif 9 to hit him, it should be +3 dif yes? So dif 8 for a bite or razor claws. Dif 8 isn't that hard.<br /> 3) any high ranking combat fera character worth their rank can take 12 dice of Agg. That really isn't that impressive.<br /> 4) Totem Form covers the &quot;big spirit to face him&quot; big I would think.<br /> 5) I looked up the Shivasakti avatar war form thing and stats-wise it isn't terribly impressive. 8/6/7 physicals with Brawl 6 and Dodge (Athletics now 4), 6 in each Mental attributes. No melee. So I know that a Mage's stats in general aren't what make them powerful, but this is what you are saying gives him &quot;at least 16 dice&quot;? How? and Zhyzak is homid form is almost as strong.<br /> <br /> This is just my impression but having read through Voormas' story, most/all of his feats (just like most story characters) are pure metaplot silliness without any real system to back it up.<br /> <br /> Like I said in the beginning, I'm not saying your special snowflake Mage character can't (or shouldn't) win. But it certainly doesn't seem as simple as that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:10:20-07:00","id":967384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967318#post967318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying your Mage icon should be defeated but there are some points above worth disputing.<br /> 1) As of M20, doesn't every supernatural creature with an occult rating get countermagic? Attacking a Caern/Pit then puts a serious cramp in the effects being thrown around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in this case, Night-folk countermagick has limits<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;On a related note,<b> the Night-Folk cannot counter immediate-damage attacks like plasma bolts or Enlightened martial<br /> arts, nor can they oppose indirect assaults like weakened floors, fire, typhoons, and so forth. </b>The only way to counter<br /> a mage\u2019s attack is to recognize it as a mystic assault. Thaumaturgical counterspells won\u2019t prevent a Virtual Adept from<br /> using Enlightened hypertech to hack the vampire prince\u2019s bank account. &quot;<br /> <br /> Countermagick works only on effects working direcltly ON you, like teleporting, or shapeshifting.<br /> Innate countermagic will not protect you against a blast of magic energy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) It's not dif 9 to hit him, it should be +3 dif yes? So dif 8 for a bite or razor claws. Dif 8 isn't that hard. </div> </div> </div>It's still difficult 8 with 11 dices agaisnt someone who dodges with 6 with at least 16 dices so the chances would be really against you.<br /> Even more, if Voormas chooses to play defensive he could even discard the +3 attack bonus for a -3 difficult at dodge/parry/block or whatever he prefers.<br /> So you'd have Zhyzhak who use 11 dices and hits at 8, and Voormas who uses 16 dices and dodges at 3.<br /> Which means that it's practically impossible for Zhyzhak to hit Voormas in close fight.<br /> While for Vormaas is not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) any high ranking combat fera character worth their rank can take 12 dice of Agg. That really isn't that impressive. </div> </div> </div>Ah, they can even soak damages from silver? Because I don't remember Zhyzhak having a gift to soak silver (from a creature who has STR 8, +2 for the swords, and adds the extra-success of a16 dices of attack.<br /> With Arete 9,24 point of quintessence and matter 3 anything Voormas gets his hands on can be turned in silver in no time and with great ease.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) Totem Form covers the &quot;big spirit to face him&quot; big I would think. </div> </div> </div><br /> That's true, that's her best chance, if she call her totem for help she can manage it, but again the above mentioned totem is gonna fight an Archmage with arete 9 who mastered the Spirit sphere.<br /> <br /> Now I should check in the book of the wyrm if there were stats for the Green Dragon (I think there was something) because with her Totem background she has not a powerful Totem, if we stick to the rule of Totem creation.<br /> Let's even says her Totem is made only for battle, she has a 20 point totem, which could mean...I don't know, 10 points for attributes and 10 points for charms.<br /> <br /> That means her Totem would have 30 point he can divide beetween Rage,Gnosis and Willpower, and he would have 5 charms.<br /> It would be a spirit much less powerful than Fenris war avatar, much less powerful.<br /> It would be more or less like a Nexus Crawler.<br /> <br /> But again, I should check, because I could swear that the Green Dragon was statted somewhere...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) I looked up the Shivasakti avatar war form thing and stats-wise it isn't terribly impressive. 8/6/7 physicals with Brawl 6 and Dodge (Athletics now 4), 6 in each Mental attributes. No melee. So I know that a Mage's stats in general aren't what make them powerful, but this is what you are saying gives him &quot;at least 16 dice&quot;? How? and Zhyzak is homid form is almost as strong. </div> </div> </div><br /> He has Melee 6, specialized in Swords<br /> From Ascension book, page 88<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Abilities</b><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">: Academics 5 (India), Alertness 4, Awareness 6 (Entropic Magic), Brawl 6 (Pressure Points), Cosmology 5 (Entropic Realms), Dodge 4 (Dodging while striking), Enigmas 5 (Cosmological), Etiquette 3, Intimidation 6 (In Avatar Form), Investigation 5 (No Tools), Leadership 5 (Over Followers), Medicine 4 ,</span></span></span>Meditation 6 (Mantras), Melee 6 (Swords), Occult 6 (Thanatoic), Stealth 6 (Shadowing), Subterfuge 5 (Easy Liar)&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And he has extra dices in his war form<br /> <br /> &quot;<br /> Attributes before the slash represent the weakest version of his Avatar form. The strong form adds at least four dice to unarmed or melee combat pools, soaks lethal and aggravated wounds and radiates an aura of fear (roll Willpower, difficulty 6 to overcome; at least three successes are required). Voormas might have 20 or more successes worth of additional Effects prepared. These spells do tax his concentration, just as they would for any other mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> (so dexterity 6 +Melee 6+3 extra dices= 16)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> and four dices at least, because in the original rotes that gave Voormas that form (Iron Avatar rote, Euthanatos book), the iron avatar can easily have 6,8 or more extra dices,4 dices was the minimum the original rotes allowed, so he could easily use 18 or 20 dices and it would be not a exaggeration.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then again someone could say the extra dices involve unarmed and melee combat, so they do not applies to dodge, but it's not a problem, you just make him parry instead of dodge, it's really the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Even more, with that much quintessence (24) he could easily heal anything you do to him.<br /> Healing agg takes life 3, with that much quintessence and arete 9 he has probably the highest healing potential in the whole world of darkness, and since he already has the most severe form of jhor he has no qualms in replaining his reserves by draining quintessence from his foe in the fight with a Vampire-Chi strike.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is just my impression but having read through Voormas' story, most/all of his feats (just like most story characters) are pure metaplot silliness without any real system to back it up. </div> </div> </div><br /> He is the second highest statted character in Mage the Ascension, just a step below The Unnamed, who is the most powerful among the Aswadim, and with those stats,those spheres and that ammount of prepared effects there is little he can't do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:02:45-07:00","id":967409,"title":"","content":"First, thank you for the additional information. There was a point or 2 I had missed in skimming over Voormas obviously.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967384#post967384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in this case, Night-folk countermagick has limits<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;On a related note,<b> the Night-Folk cannot counter immediate-damage attacks like plasma bolts or Enlightened martial<br /> arts, nor can they oppose indirect assaults like weakened floors, fire, typhoons, and so forth. </b>The only way to counter<br /> a mage\u2019s attack is to recognize it as a mystic assault. Thaumaturgical counterspells won\u2019t prevent a Virtual Adept from<br /> using Enlightened hypertech to hack the vampire prince\u2019s bank account. &quot;<br /> <br /> Countermagick works only on effects working direcltly ON you, like teleporting, or shapeshifting.<br /> Innate countermagic will not protect you against a blast of magic energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Though none of the tactics presented rely on it, so I would guess that countermagic won't come into this at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967384#post967384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still difficult 8 with 11 dices agaisnt someone us dodge with 6 with at least 16 so the chances would be really against you.<br /> Even more, if Voormas chooses to play defensive he could even discard the plus +3 attack bonus for a -3 dodge difficult.<br /> So you'd have Zhyzhak who use 11 dices and hits at 8, and Voormas who uses 16 dices and dodges at 3.<br /> Which means that it's practically impossible for Zhyzhak to hit Voormas in close fight.<br /> While for Vormaas is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Voormas is going to need to either split dice pools or use Time effects (which are horribly inefficient) to keep up with Zhyzhak. Just having higher dice pools (regardless of dif) doesn't mean you win in a fight, when extra actions are a factor. Also worth noting (and this is a big deal) the proposed scenario had Voormas attacking the Trinity Caern Hive. The Hive is home to a few dozen Spirals. So this isn;t a fight vs Zhyzhak. This is a fight against a Caern. And there isn't any real way to tell which Garou that are fighting are the higher ranking ones, and thus more magically dangerous. (Keep in mind I didn't make the claim that Zhyzhak would kill Voormas, I just came into this after). Also included would be the Caern itself fighting (The Spirit, and the Thunderwyrm it resides in) and whatever other creatures are there (possible fomori and other guardian spirits, etc).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967384#post967384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah, they can even soak damages from silver? Because I don't remember Zhyzhak having a gift to soak silver (from a creature who has STR 8, +2 for the swords, and adds the extra-success of a16 dices of attack</div> </div> </div> </div> If Voormas attacks with a full dice pool, he is almost certainly dead from incoming attacks. That being said, she doesn't seem a to have a means of soak against silver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967384#post967384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true, that's her best chance, if she call her totem for help she can manage it, but again the above mentioned totem is gonna fight an Archmage with arete 9 who mastered the Spirit sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I was referring to a Gift. Her Totem will also probably be involved though since you brought it up. Again, this is far from a 1 on 1 fight. I always find it interesting when people reduce cross splat conflicts to one on one fights between characters mentioned. And usually that's why Werewolf gets the short end of the stick. (imo) you arent supposed to compare a Methuselah or Arch-mage to a Garou. You should be comparing them to a Pack because that's how the different games function. And again, in this scenario, it was set up as Voormas attacking a Trinity Caern Hive. Zhyzhak is it's Champion, but she is far from the only high ranking Garou there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967384#post967384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I should check in the book of the wyrm if there were stats for the Green Dragon (I think there was something) because with her Totem background she has not a powerful Totem, if we stick to the rule of Totem creation.<br /> Let's even says her Totem is made only for battle, she has a 20 point totem, which could mean...I don't know, 10 points for attributes and 10 points for charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> That means her Totem would have 30 point he can divide beetween Rage,Gnosis and Willpower, and he would have 5 charms.<br /> It would be a spirit much less powerful than Fenris war avatar, much less powerful.<br /> It would be more or less like a Nexus Crawler.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that's not actually entirely how that works. The point distribution is for the Totem Avatar (a Gaffling or Jaggling) that guides the pack, or in this case individual. That Spirit is going to 100% be involved in this. Not the Incarna, which is what I took from you saying ask her Totem for help. Totem Form (or Avatar of the Wyrm) is functionally different. But again, the pure stats don't matter as much. The Charms it have will be much more important. For 5 essence points a Nexus Crawler pretty much wins regardless of other stats.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967384#post967384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He has Melee 6, specialized in Swords<br /> From Ascension book, page 88<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Abilities</b><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">: Academics 5 (India), Alertness 4, Awareness 6 (Entropic Magic), Brawl 6 (Pressure Points), Cosmology 5 (Entropic Realms), Dodge 4 (Dodging while striking), Enigmas 5 (Cosmological), Etiquette 3, Intimidation 6 (In Avatar Form), Investigation 5 (No Tools), Leadership 5 (Over Followers), Medicine 4 ,</span></span></span>Meditation 6 (Mantras), Melee 6 (Swords), Occult 6 (Thanatoic), Stealth 6 (Shadowing), Subterfuge 5 (Easy Liar)&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And he has extra dices in his war form<br /> <br /> &quot;Attributes before the slash represent the weakest version of his Avatar form. The strong form adds at least four dice to unarmed or melee combat pools, soaks lethal and aggravated wounds and radiates an aura of fear (roll Willpower, difficulty 6 to overcome; at least three successes are required). Voormas might have 20 or more successes worth of additional Effects prepared. These spells do tax his concentration, just as they would for any other mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> (so dexterity 6 +Melee 6+3 extra dices= 16)</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't make much sense to me to have additional dice added that could have been included in the form stats, but hey that's Mage for you. I missed the Melee stat and that portion of his form extras. Apologies. I had read it as the stats being higher and thus have added &quot;at least 4 dice&quot;, not add 4 dice on top of the increased dice the block already mentioned.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:44:21-07:00","id":967470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967409#post967409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, thank you for the additional information. There was a point or 2 I had missed in skimming over Voormas obviously.<br /> <br /> Okay. Though none of the tactics presented rely on it, so I would guess that countermagic won't come into this at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Voormas is going to need to either split dice pools or use Time effects (which are horribly inefficient) to keep up with Zhyzhak. Just having higher dice pools (regardless of dif) doesn't mean you win in a fight, when extra actions are a factor</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well extra-actions may be not be a factor at all, because the easiest thing Voormas can do to prevent Zhyzhak from using extra-actions is the old strategy Force mages uses against Elders with Celerity in fight: Casting the Friction Curse with force 3, which will prevent her from using extra-actions with rage, while he will still be able to use extra-actions with Time 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also worth noting (and this is a big deal) the proposed scenario had Voormas attacking the Trinity Caern Hive. The Hive is home to a few dozen Spirals. So this isn;t a fight vs Zhyzhak. This is a fight against a Caern. And there isn't any real way to tell which Garou that are fighting are the higher ranking ones, and thus more magically dangerous. (Keep in mind I didn't make the claim that Zhyzhak would kill Voormas, I just came into this after). Also included would be the Caern itself fighting (The Spirit, and the Thunderwyrm it resides in) and whatever other creatures are there (possible fomori and other guardian spirits, etc).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...Actually, I was referring to a Gift. Her Totem will also probably be involved though since you brought it up. Again, this is far from a 1 on 1 fight. I always find it interesting when people reduce cross splat conflicts to one on one fights between characters mentioned. And usually that's why Werewolf gets the short end of the stick. (imo) you arent supposed to compare a Methuselah or Arch-mage to a Garou. You should be comparing them to a Pack because that's how the different games function. And again, in this scenario, it was set up as Voormas attacking a Trinity Caern Hive. Zhyzhak is it's Champion, but she is far from the only high ranking Garou there. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Obviusly I'm talking of a white room contest, there is no doubt that circumstances might completely change the course of the battle, for the same reason a great group of neonates can take down an elder vampires or for the same reason a pack of werewolves who relies on cunning and pack tactics can bring down a Nexus Crawler: contest is everything, but again I was working on a white room hypotesis.<br /> <br /> Then again, if we work on contest we must remember that Voormas is not alone.<br /> He is dispotic leader of an entire confraternity of mages, the Consaguinity of Eternal Joy, which is composed by 12 experienced Euthanatos killers, and none of them deals in research or anything else, they are just assassins specialized in combat.<br /> Moreover Voormas has some really mighty allies (he has Allies 10), one of them being Yama Queen Touh Mouh, so he could also relies on Akumas and wraiths if needed.<br /> So again, let's remember that contest might works in both directions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Keep in mind I didn't make the claim that Zhyzhak would kill Voormas, I just came into this after) </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> About this I'd like to make this clear: I didn't wanted to start a confrontation,I just said that is a matter of fact that many caerns have been conquered by mages, and many are too heavily defended to be retaken.<br /> <br /> Which by the way is true also in Werewolves books<br /> <br /> W20 p310<br /> <br /> &quot;Mages and marauding spirits sometimes want to feast on<br /> (or despoil) these pure and powerful places. Garou vigilantly<br /> guard caerns, not only to preserve the undiluted<br /> essence of the Wyld, but also to sustain the Garou Nation.<br /> Unfortunately, werewolves are losing that fight. Precious<br /> few Garou caerns remain. Their cause is so desperate that<br /> some packs attempt to create urban caerns.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> It's a matter of lore that Werewolves are failing to protect Caerns, not even by their fault, but because they are surrounded by raiders.<br /> <br /> Then Sauer entered claiming Zhyzhak would easily crush the skull of one of the most powerful Archmage (no, the MOST powerful Archmage) of the modern era.<br /> Which is not , in a one on one against Paramaguru you really need something bigger, Fenris war avatar or Simoon should do the trick, a mortal werewolf,even if he is the most powerful werewolf since the War of rage, is not enough.<br /> <br /> And that is not strange, is normal: in Werewolf the most powerful creatures are not the werewolves themselves, the upper eschelon of the &quot;OMG that's big&quot; scale has always been claimed by the spirits, just as in Vampire has always been claimed by methuselah and in Mage by archmages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So that's not actually entirely how that works. The point distribution is for the Totem Avatar (a Gaffling or Jaggling) that guides the pack, or in this case individual. That Spirit is going to 100% be involved in this. Not the Incarna, which is what I took from you saying ask her Totem for help. Totem Form (or Avatar of the Wyrm) is functionally different. But again, the pure stats don't matter as much. The Charms it have will be much more important. For 5 essence points a Nexus Crawler pretty much wins regardless of other stats. </div> </div> </div>Ah sorry, I misunderstood, I tought you were talking about her Totem background.<br /> I'll check, since I don't remember how the above mentioned gift works.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT.<br /> <br /> Ok, found it.<br /> <br /> Yeah pretty impressive, she could turn in something as powerful as an archid, but still it would be not a wise strategy, because Voormas could turn her back to homid form.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shapechanging Shapechangers<br /> Generally, it\u2019s not wise to try to change shapechanging Night-Folk into other shapes. Werewolves, spirits, shapeshifting<br /> mages, and other creatures with an essentially innate ability to change their forms can usually shift back to their natural<br /> forms at will (as with werecreatures), or else use their Arts to change as they Will (as with mages).<br /> <b>That said, a mage with Spirit 3 and Life 4 or higher can force a werecreature to remain in its current form for the duration<br /> of the Effect, or else send her into one of her other forms for a similar time.</b> Needless to say, the feral-folk do not enjoy<br /> being jerked around by some wise-ass mage, and they tend to view such transformations\u2026 poorly.<br /> Certain creatures, such as vampires with form-changing Disciplines like Protean and Vicissitude, may shift shape through<br /> their own innate powers. Although such changes often require expenditures of blood or other resources, those Night-Folk<br /> won\u2019t remain bound by some mage\u2019s antics for long\u2026<br /> For details about the necessary Spheres and the innate resistance&quot;<br /> <br /> So either he prevents her from changing, either he turns her in homid after the change, and since Totem Form requires an entire turn he has all the time he needs to cast it,<br /> Here countermagick would come in place, problem is Zhyzhak has 9 dice of countermagic, which is a lot sure, but her difficult to perform it would be 9, since for the Night-Folk the difficult for countermagick is determined by the Arete of the mage (if above 7, otherwise the base difficult is 7).<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, that would be a nice trick Voormas could use with his 20 success of prepared effects: a 10 success effect that prevents the enemy from shapeshifting.<br /> This way Zhyzhak would have to fight Voormas in Homid form.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't make much sense to me to have additional dice added that could have been included in the form stats, but hey that's Mage for you. I missed the Melee stat and that portion of his form extras. Apologies. I had read it as the stats being higher and thus have added &quot;at least 4 dice&quot;, not add 4 dice on top of the increased dice the block already mentioned. </div> </div> </div>The extra dices are caused from the extra-arms the Iron Avatar can give you (In this form Voormas has six arms).<br /> <br /> <br /> From the Euthanatos book (reminds that while the final effect is the same Voormas doesn't need to cast the rote anymore to became the Avatar, he has just embodied it, the Iron Avatar is just the manifestation of his avatar now)<br /> <br /> Regarding the extra-dices<br /> <br /> &quot;These arms add four additional dice to the mage's unarmed and Melee dice pools, though each extra success can be used to enhanche co-ordination (adding an additional two dice to armed and unarmed combat dce pools per success)&quot;.<br /> <br /> So since it's two extra-dices per success it can easily be far greater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:31:57-07:00","id":967652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967470#post967470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well...</div> </div> </div> </div>She's the chosen of the Green Dragon. If Mage bullshit comes into play, this status kills the Mage bullshit. End of story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:43:47-07:00","id":967659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967652#post967652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She's the chosen of the Green Dragon. If Mage bullshit comes into play, this status kills the Mage bullshit. End of story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah yeah, because you say so.<br /> <br /> Sorry can you tell me at what page can I find this rule?<br /> <br /> Ah a most interesting rule, really, somehow still I must have missed it.<br /> <br /> Page pls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:02:08-07:00","id":967693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967470#post967470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well extra-actions may be not be a factor at all, because the easiest thing Voormas can do to prevent Zhyzhak from using extra-actions is the old strategy Force mages uses against Elders with Celerity in fight: Casting the Friction Curse with force 3, which will prevent her from using extra-actions with rage, while he will still be able to use extra-actions with Time 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the Friction Curse idea thrown around a lot. Couple of points on this. Countermagic will work against it. It is generally horribly systemed in game, and it does heat damage which ends up being bashing to Zhyzhak due to Master of Fire. Also (skipping ahead a little) a lot of the arguments are X effect for Y situation. Action economy-wise, he's only casting 1 effect at a time and he may or may not get enough successes for it to be meaningful. Even Archmages rely on ritual casting to get enough successes. How many successes to change into the greater war form? He shows up in the story he's in because of hand wavy Mage stuff. That is also why he gets free 20 successes of effects hanging around to do whatever he wants.<br /> <br /> What does this line mean btw: &quot;<i>These spells do tax his concentration, just as they would for any other mage.&quot;?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967470#post967470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviusly I'm talking of a white room contest, there is no doubt that circumstances might completely change the course of the battle, for the same reason a great group of neonates can take down an elder vampires or for the same reason a pack of werewolves who relies on cunning and pack tactics can bring down a Nexus Crawler: contest is everything, but again I was working on a white room hypotesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw that we were having different comparisons so tried to clarify at least what I was saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967470#post967470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then again, if we work on contest we must remember that Voormas is not alone.<br /> He is dispotic leader of an entire confraternity of mages, the Consaguinity of Eternal Joy, which is composed by 12 experienced Euthanatos killers, and none of them deals in research or anything else, they are just assassins specialized in combat.<br /> Moreover Voormas has some really mighty allies (he has Allies 10), one of them being Yama Queen Touh Mouh, so he could also relies on Akumas and wraiths if needed.<br /> So again, let's remember that contest might works in both directions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that the Yama Queen he ate? And Allies 10 doesn't matter much to me. Backgrounds like that are thrown on characters without much thought about what they actually do. Baba Yaga doesn't have any contacts or allies and only has 3 retainers and she has access to silly amounts of creatures in her army. I would say Allies 10 is easily outdone by the resources of one of the largest (probably the largest) Hive. But at that point the speculation level is getting beyond being able to discuss..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967470#post967470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> About this I'd like to make this clear: I didn't wanted to start a confrontation,I just said that is a matter of fact that many caerns have been conquered by mages, and many are too heavily defended to be retaken.<br /> <br /> Which by the way is true also in Werewolves books<br /> <br /> W20 p310<br /> <br /> &quot;Mages and marauding spirits sometimes want to feast on<br /> (or despoil) these pure and powerful places. Garou vigilantly<br /> guard caerns, not only to preserve the undiluted<br /> essence of the Wyld, but also to sustain the Garou Nation.<br /> Unfortunately, werewolves are losing that fight. Precious<br /> few Garou caerns remain. Their cause is so desperate that<br /> some packs attempt to create urban caerns.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> It's a matter of lore that Werewolves are failing to protect Caerns, not even by their fault, but because they are surrounded by raiders.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has little to do with Mages actually. At least in setting. Garou are losing Caerns because they have about or less than half the population to fill/defend them. And that (again) has nothing to do with Mages. It's all about this being the End Times and the world being on the cusp of the Apocalypse. It's a setting feature.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967470#post967470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah sorry, I misunderstood, I tought you were talking about her Totem background.<br /> I'll check, since I don't remember how the above mentioned gift works.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT.<br /> <br /> Ok, found it.<br /> <br /> Yeah pretty impressive, she could turn in something as powerful as an archid, but still it would be not a wise strategy, because Voormas could turn her back to homid form.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Avatar of the Wyrm is kind of pathetic for a 5th Rank Gift (system-wise), which is why I'm guessing it didn't get reprinted in W20. I was thinking a lot more like Totem Form operates, which is ST fiat aspects of the Totem (which would likewise be immune-ish to the effect detailed below).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967470#post967470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Shapechanging Shapechangers<br /> Generally, it\u2019s not wise to try to change shapechanging Night-Folk into other shapes. Werewolves, spirits, shapeshifting<br /> mages, and other creatures with an essentially innate ability to change their forms can usually shift back to their natural<br /> forms at will (as with werecreatures), or else use their Arts to change as they Will (as with mages).<br /> <b>That said, a mage with Spirit 3 and Life 4 or higher can force a werecreature to remain in its current form for the duration<br /> of the Effect, or else send her into one of her other forms for a similar time.</b> Needless to say, the feral-folk do not enjoy<br /> being jerked around by some wise-ass mage, and they tend to view such transformations\u2026 poorly.<br /> Certain creatures, such as vampires with form-changing Disciplines like Protean and Vicissitude, may shift shape through<br /> their own innate powers. Although such changes often require expenditures of blood or other resources, those Night-Folk<br /> won\u2019t remain bound by some mage\u2019s antics for long\u2026<br /> For details about the necessary Spheres and the innate resistance&quot;<br /> <br /> So either he prevents her from changing, either he turns her in homid after the change, and since Totem Form requires an entire turn he has all the time he needs to cast it,<br /> Here countermagick would come in place, problem is Zhyzhak has 9 dice of countermagic, which is a lot sure, but her difficult to perform it would be 9, since for the Night-Folk the difficult for countermagick is determined by the Arete of the mage (if above 7, otherwise the base difficult is 7).</div> </div> </div> </div> Totem Form isn't shapeshifting. It is channeling the raw essence of an Incarna. I don't actually think that effect would work. Voormas would be forced to try something with a much higher level of Spirit. And whether or not he can get enough successes is actually debatable, even with his high Arete rating. But if he did attempt it and found out it didn't work, he will have wasted a turn trying.<br /> <br /> That's actually another thing that I see a lot. Tailored effects for the target, without the target knowing an effect would require certain spheres. So how does that work from that point? Like if you try the effect above but it would require Spirit 5 instead of 3, the effect auto-fails doesn't it? (this is an actual question I have, not a criticism)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967470#post967470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now that I think about it, that would be a nice trick Voormas could use with his 20 success of prepared effects: a 10 success effect that prevents the enemy from shapeshifting.<br /> This way Zhyzhak would have to fight Voormas in Homid form.</div> </div> </div> </div> Her Crinos and Homid forms differ but her Homid form is quite impressive in its own right. That would possible be a waste of half of his built up effect successes. And Take the True Form would probably work just the same on him, though Voormas ends up and a fairly scrawny old man from that effect (assuming it wasn't countermagic'd).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967470#post967470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the Euthanatos book (reminds that while the final effect is the same Voormas doesn't need to cast the rote anymore to became the Avatar, he has just embodied it, the Iron Avatar is just the manifestation of his avatar now)<br /> <br /> Regarding the extra-dices<br /> <br /> &quot;These arms add four additional dice to the mage's unarmed and Melee dice pools, though each extra success can be used to enhanche co-ordination (adding an additional two dice to armed and unarmed combat dce pools per success)&quot;.<br /> <br /> So since it's two extra-dices per success it can easily be far greater.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actual question. greater than 4 how? you just said he doesn't roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967659#post967659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah yeah, because you say so.<br /> <br /> Sorry can you tell me at what page can I find this rule?<br /> <br /> Ah a most interesting rule, really, somehow still I must have missed it.<br /> <br /> Page pls?</div> </div> </div> </div>His logic does hold up for a Werewolf game actually. It's a matter of themes. Being condescending though doesn't help conversation at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the questions I had from your post:<br /> 1) how does concentration and held effects actually work. (referring to the 20 successes of spells which tax his concentration)<br /> 1b) Are you deciding what those effects are as they become helpful? I get the impression that for the scenario he's used in, that's exactly why they're there.<br /> 2) if you find out you didn't use the right Sphere levels, does a casting just fail outright?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:10:17-07:00","id":967734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967659#post967659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah yeah, because you say so.<br /> <br /> Sorry can you tell me at what page can I find this rule?<br /> <br /> Ah a most interesting rule, really, somehow still I must have missed it.<br /> <br /> Page pls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Observe the differences between her game stats in Caerns: Places of Power, Rage: Warriors of the Apocalypse, and finally, in Apocalypse. Between them, the conception of her power changed dramatically, from being an unusually-fluffed Strength and Stamina of 5 to having superhuman might and resilience while still in Homid. That's by no means the end of the road; it wouldn't be out of place to give her stats even higher in W20. Apocalypse is more like a basement presentation, and the prior writeups and sub-basements, none really tapping into the plot device powering that champion of corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T04:25:46-07:00","id":967859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967693#post967693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see the Friction Curse idea thrown around a lot. Couple of points on this. Countermagic will work against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it will, but remember that the more powerful the mage the more difficult countermagic is: countermagic has a base difficult of 7, but if the mage arete is higher than 7 than the base difficult is his Arete, and in Voormas case is 9.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is generally horribly systemed in game, and it does heat damage which ends up being bashing to Zhyzhak due to Master of Fire. Also (skipping ahead a little) a lot of the arguments are X effect for Y situation. Action economy-wise, he's only casting 1 effect at a time and he may or may not get enough successes for it to be meaningful. Even Archmages rely on ritual casting to get enough successes. </div> </div> </div>Indeed but remember that friction curse is Force 3 effect (I'd say a vulgar one), which means a base difficult of 7, Voormas has an uncanny 24 quintessence rating, so he can easily spend 3 point of quintessence to make it at difficult 4.<br /> If you are rolling 9 dices at difficult 4 you have pretty high chances to get all the success you need in one roll, remember that friction curse doesn't require many success, it's by all means a minor feat (it would require probably 3 success, like casting a fireball I think).<br /> So while what you are saying is true for most mages (the common mage has arete 4, so even a 3 success spell is hard to cast) it's not true for Voormas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [QUOTE]How many successes to change into the greater war form? He shows up in the story he's in because of hand wavy Mage stuff. That is also why he gets free 20 successes of effects hanging around to do whatever he wants.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> 30 success at base difficult 8, but again, with arete 9 an all that quintessence is far from a taxing feat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does this line mean btw: &quot;<i>These spells do tax his concentration, just as they would for any other mage.&quot;?</i> </div> </div> </div>Each two runnings effect for a mage add +1 to the base difficult of a spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't that the Yama Queen he ate? And Allies 10 doesn't matter much to me. Backgrounds like that are thrown on characters without much thought about what they actually do. Baba Yaga doesn't have any contacts or allies and only has 3 retainers and she has access to silly amounts of creatures in her army. I would say Allies 10 is easily outdone by the resources of one of the largest (probably the largest) Hive. But at that point the speculation level is getting beyond being able to discuss.. </div> </div> </div>Well that Allies 10 is pretty much accurate: Voormas commands an army.<br /> In Ascension he had the whole resources of the Hell of Being Skinned Alive, and threwed legions of akuma, wraiths,mages and liches at the gates of Cerberus,he controlled hundreds of hellish creatures called Pretas, and the the Yamasttvas, the Liches of the Idran (the same that help the Black Hand).<br /> After he concquered Cerberus his forces were big enough to fend off all the Nephandic armies who tried to stop him.<br /> <br /> So technically speaking allies 10 is not even trully representative of the forces he can muster.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Totem Form isn't shapeshifting. It is channeling the raw essence of an Incarna. I don't actually think that effect would work. Voormas would be forced to try something with a much higher level of Spirit. And whether or not he can get enough successes is actually debatable, even with his high Arete rating. But if he did attempt it and found out it didn't work, he will have wasted a turn trying. </div> </div> </div>That's true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's actually another thing that I see a lot. Tailored effects for the target, without the target knowing an effect would require certain spheres. So how does that work from that point? Like if you try the effect above but it would require Spirit 5 instead of 3, the effect auto-fails doesn't it? (this is an actual question I have, not a criticism) </div> </div> </div><br /> You see...there is a big difference between the meta-game magic and the in-game magic.<br /> Arete is not just your skill in casting spell, is also your comprension of magic and the world that surrounds you.<br /> <br /> Then there are spheres, remember that spheres are not like you know them in meta-game, each Tradition and Convention has its own view of the spheres and learning a sphere doesn't simply require spending xp, but studying,there is a lot of academia involved.<br /> So a mage knows what sphere he should use, because he studied the theory of the spheres, he has been trained by masters and has studied the subject<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Her Crinos and Homid forms differ but her Homid form is quite impressive in its own right. That would possible be a waste of half of his built up effect successes. And Take the True Form would probably work just the same on him, though Voormas ends up and a fairly scrawny old man from that effect (assuming it wasn't countermagic'd). </div> </div> </div>True<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actual question. greater than 4 how? you just said he doesn't roll. </div> </div> </div><br /> Voormas embodied this Avatar form, the Iron Avatar is now just a part of him, so he doesn't need to roll anymore, it's like a permanent effect he can call anythime he wants<br /> Now in the original rote how many extra dices you'd get was a choice determined by the player.<br /> So nothing stops you from establishing that in his original roll Voormas put more success in the arms effect, as the Euthanatos book suggests.<br /> So since an Iron Avatar can have 4.6.8 extra dices Voormas war form also can have it, it's up to you, this is why the description says that he has 4 dice at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His logic does hold up for a Werewolf game actually. It's a matter of themes. Being condescending though doesn't help conversation at all. </div> </div> </div>Yeah you know but you are discussing a topic, you are spilling a lot of ink,comparing rules,system at all, and then someone enters the topic ignoring all that was written, all that was debated and says &quot;gne gne! He dies 'cause I say so, fuck the rules&quot;<br /> <br /> It's frustrating at best, depressing at worst.<br /> <br /> And even there no, it doesn't hold up, because Zhyzhak is a statted character.<br /> Is not a fiat character like a Maeljin or an Incarna.<br /> Is statted,then killable by players, in Apocalypse it is even said that a pack of rank 4 or 5 can take her down, so yes, it's killable.<br /> <br /> It's not Ur-Shulgi that is not statted, is not Dante that is not statted, is not the Lord of pain that is not statted, Zhyzhak is a statted character that can be killed, had the writers tought she was beyond the killing she would have not been statted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> So the questions I had from your post:<br /> 1) how does concentration and held effects actually work. (referring to the 20 successes of spells which tax his concentration) </div> </div> </div>As I said, every 2 effect active add 1 to the base difficult of a spell.<br /> This means that for a mage is better either spending a lot of time in preparation and use few spell later, or do not prepare in order to better adapt to the situation.<br /> But, even here, it depends on who you are: if you are a mage who has big Arete dice pool and a lot of quintessence you can easily overcome this limitations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1b) Are you deciding what those effects are as they become helpful? I get the impression that for the scenario he's used in, that's exactly why they're there. </div> </div> </div>An honest master should decide what those effect are before the fight, and not chainging them after that.<br /> Obviously this requires from the master a lot of study on the subject to be fully effective.<br /> Just look above, at start I considered using a Entropy 1 effect to get -3 at the attack difficult, after a second tought and your explanation now I would use a Time 2 effect to have -3 at the dodge difficult.<br /> <br /> If the master has studied well the subject the prepared effect, even without changing them, can be really effective, if he was lazy the advantage of the prepared effect could be jeopardized.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) if you find out you didn't use the right Sphere levels, does a casting just fail outright?<br /> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you do not have the right sphere level you can't even cast it,because as I said before not having the right sphere levels in-game doesn't mean you used the wrong sphere, it means you have no idea how to pull out that effect.<br /> Remember that before you roll an effect you need the approval of the master, so if the master knows that you do not have the right spheres you will be able to do the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:33:35-07:00","id":968047,"title":"","content":"Your Quote formatting was a bit all over the place on this one (I think you misses a close Quote or 2) so I will do my best with responses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967859#post967859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed but remember that friction curse is Force 3 effect (I'd say a vulgar one), which means a base difficult of 7, Voormas has an uncanny 24 quintessence rating, so he can easily spend 3 point of quintessence to make it at difficult 4.<br /> If you are rolling 9 dices at difficult 4 you have pretty high chances to get all the success you need in one roll, remember that friction curse doesn't require many success, it's by all means a minor feat (it would require probably 3 success, like casting a fireball I think).<br /> So while what you are saying is true for most mages (the common mage has arete 4, so even a 3 success spell is hard to cast) it's not true for Voormas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dif 4 +1 for every 2 other ongoing or delayed effects isn't it? So possibly higher? And what is the actual system for Friction Curse? I could only find a description of the effect without any actual crunch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967859#post967859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well that Allies 10 is pretty much accurate: Voormas commands an army.<br /> In Ascension he had the whole resources of the Hell of Being Skinned Alive, and threwed legions of akuma, wraiths,mages and liches at the gates of Cerberus,he controlled hundreds of hellish creatures called Pretas, and the the Yamasttvas, the Liches of the Idran (the same that help the Black Hand).<br /> After he concquered Cerberus his forces were big enough to fend off all the Nephandic armies who tried to stop him.<br /> <br /> So technically speaking allies 10 is not even trully representative of the forces he can muster.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same can be said of Zhyzhak (who has no Allies background to speak of), so best to skip over this. She is 1 of 3 contenders for leading all of the Spirals (in the Apocalypse scenarios) and even if she only got 1/3 of them to her call that's at least 1000-1500 Spirals along with Banes and Fomori and other stuff. I feel like going out to those lengths makes this conversation more pointless though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967859#post967859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You see...there is a big difference between the meta-game magic and the in-game magic.<br /> Arete is not just your skill in casting spell, is also your comprension of magic and the world that surrounds you.<br /> <br /> Then there are spheres, remember that spheres are not like you know them in meta-game, each Tradition and Convention has its own view of the spheres and learning a sphere doesn't simply require spending xp, but studying,there is a lot of academia involved.<br /> So a mage knows what sphere he should use, because he studied the theory of the spheres, he has been trained by masters and has studied the subject</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that this is actually true. If you are a Mage and you try and use Rip the Man Body (Life 3) on what you think is a human, you should be attempting the magick, only to find out after the fact that the creature you attempted your magick on was a Vampire/Garou/etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967859#post967859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voormas embodied this Avatar form, the Iron Avatar is now just a part of him, so he doesn't need to roll anymore, it's like a permanent effect he can call anythime he wants<br /> Now in the original rote how many extra dices you'd get was a choice determined by the player.<br /> So nothing stops you from establishing that in his original roll Voormas put more success in the arms effect, as the Euthanatos book suggests.<br /> So since an Iron Avatar can have 4.6.8 extra dices Voormas war form also can have it, it's up to you, this is why the description says that he has 4 dice at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>So 4 dice then since that's what it describes. Their wording is weird since it says &quot;at least&quot;, but if he isn't casting ti anymore I would stick with the base minimum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967859#post967859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah you know but you are discussing a topic, you are spilling a lot of ink,comparing rules,system at all, and then someone enters the topic ignoring all that was written, all that was debated and says &quot;gne gne! He dies 'cause I say so, fuck the rules&quot;<br /> <br /> It's frustrating at best, depressing at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have actually seen similar to that happen in a Werewolf game. A Wendigo character spent his life hunting down a Mage only to be killed (well, maimed horribly) by said Mage decades later (at Rank 4 or 5) and the player spent his Willpower and made the relevant rolls to rip out his own heart to offer it to Wendigo to get revenge. And that's precisely what happened. The Incarna showed up and that was kind of that for the Mage antagonist. I agree it isn't terribly helpful for a conversation like this, but it is thematically appropriate for a Werewolf game and so I can see why that was put forth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967859#post967859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And even there no, it doesn't hold up, because Zhyzhak is a statted character.<br /> Is not a fiat character like a Maeljin or an Incarna.<br /> Is statted,then killable by players, in Apocalypse it is even said that a pack of rank 4 or 5 can take her down, so yes, it's killable.<br /> <br /> It's not Ur-Shulgi that is not statted, is not Dante that is not statted, is not the Lord of pain that is not statted, Zhyzhak is a statted character that can be killed, had the writers tought she was beyond the killing she would have not been statted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything you just said applies to Voormas as well. Mind you, even unstated characters should be able to be killed. I don't think any character should get Plot Armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=967859#post967859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, every 2 effect active add 1 to the base difficult of a spell.<br /> This means that for a mage is better either spending a lot of time in preparation and use few spell later, or do not prepare in order to better adapt to the situation.<br /> But, even here, it depends on who you are: if you are a mage who has big Arete dice pool and a lot of quintessence you can easily overcome this limitations.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the penalties are stacking up, which is going to make any magick used less effective overall.<br /> Oh, in this scenario, you also need to set an effect aside to enter/survive the Hive, it being a radioactive pit and all. That's yet another minor thing to keep track of.<br /> <br /> <br /> After the conversation so far, going way back to what started it, I do think if Voormas attacked the Trinity Caern Hive instead of some random minor pit there is a very good chance he would be killed. It'd be an interesting fight, but that is the wrong Hive to pick for an invasion. And overall, even though Voormas has stats, as does the Hive's most prominent member (Zhyzhak) this would still fall entirely in the realm of ST fiat. There's just too much that would be thrown around to have it be anything else. And unlike Zhyzhak, Voormas would stand out as a hell of a target for Spirals to throw themselves at. Zhyzhak would just be one Garou in a wall of fur and teeth/claws and so targeting her would be much less likely (not that he would know to). The forces they can bring to the field are arguably equal (again in the realm of fiat) and so that's kind of a draw. It would come down to Voormas vs a Hive of fallen Garou. I don't think his stats and magick will overcome that disadvantage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T12:12:51-07:00","id":968067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968047#post968047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> After the conversation so far, going way back to what started it, I do think if Voormas attacked the Trinity Caern Hive instead of some random minor pit there is a very good chance he would be killed. It'd be an interesting fight, but that is the wrong Hive to pick for an invasion. And overall, even though Voormas has stats, as does the Hive's most prominent member (Zhyzhak) this would still fall entirely in the realm of ST fiat. There's just too much that would be thrown around to have it be anything else. And unlike Zhyzhak, Voormas would stand out as a hell of a target for Spirals to throw themselves at. Zhyzhak would just be one Garou in a wall of fur and teeth/claws and so targeting her would be much less likely (not that he would know to). The forces they can bring to the field are arguably equal (again in the realm of fiat) and so that's kind of a draw. It would come down to Voormas vs a Hive of fallen Garou. I don't think his stats and magick will overcome that disadvantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the Hive is in a giant thunderwyrm, sized roughly such that it wouldn't be out of place as a major threat on Arrakis, and it probably wouldn't like any attacker, much less a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T13:11:28-07:00","id":968101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968047#post968047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Quote formatting was a bit all over the place on this one (I think you misses a close Quote or 2) so I will do my best with responses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I made a mess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dif 4 +1 for every 2 other ongoing or delayed effects isn't it? So possibly higher? And what is the actual system for Friction Curse? I could only find a description of the effect without any actual crunch. </div> </div> </div>It would still be difficult 5 or 6, for an effect that could need 3 success, with 9 dices, far from impossible, against countermagic at difficulty 9.<br /> <br /> As for Friction Curse the system has never been given in detail<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Turning a subject's motion into heat energy, the mage not only renders the subject unable to move, but causes the victim to heat up until he bursts into flame! This Effect essentially turns the subject's movement into damage, so faster objects are more susceptible. A modified version can cause the subject's own breathing action to create cold, freezing the subject in place and encasing him in a block of ice. Partial successes negate some motion and impart some heat; multiple successes can transform motion into damage. Better still, since the target can't move, he is hard-pressed to dodge the ensuing eruption of fire or cold.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically it stops you, and if somehow you keep moving you are gonna suffer fire damage, the faster you are the more dire the consequences.<br /> <br /> Still since is not clear the master must establishing the working of it.<br /> If it was me, I'd say that you take 1 agg level of damage for every action you do, which means that a vampire with high levels of celerity could burst into flames if he use it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same can be said of Zhyzhak (who has no Allies background to speak of), so best to skip over this. She is 1 of 3 contenders for leading all of the Spirals (in the Apocalypse scenarios) and even if she only got 1/3 of them to her call that's at least 1000-1500 Spirals along with Banes and Fomori and other stuff. I feel like going out to those lengths makes this conversation more pointless though. </div> </div> </div>Yeah probably when it comes to allies and forces they will fight on equal terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know that this is actually true. If you are a Mage and you try and use Rip the Man Body (Life 3) on what you think is a human, you should be attempting the magick, only to find out after the fact that the creature you attempted your magick on was a Vampire/Garou/etc. </div> </div> </div>Yeah maybe it so, but it's really not difficult to understand if your foe is werecreature, every mage with Mind 1 or Spirit 1 will be able to scan an aura.<br /> So it's very unlikely that something like that could happen, maybe with a very young mage who lacks even a dot in mind or spirit, but for sure is not something that is gonna happening to an experienced mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So 4 dice then since that's what it describes. Their wording is weird since it says &quot;at least&quot;, but if he isn't casting ti anymore I would stick with the base minimum. </div> </div> </div>Yeah but they say &quot;at least&quot;, so again if a game master would present you a Voormas with 6 or 8 dices it would be not strange at all, and it would be justified by the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have actually seen similar to that happen in a Werewolf game. A Wendigo character spent his life hunting down a Mage only to be killed (well, maimed horribly) by said Mage decades later (at Rank 4 or 5) and the player spent his Willpower and made the relevant rolls to rip out his own heart to offer it to Wendigo to get revenge. And that's precisely what happened. The Incarna showed up and that was kind of that for the Mage antagonist. I agree it isn't terribly helpful for a conversation like this, but it is thematically appropriate for a Werewolf game and so I can see why that was put forth. </div> </div> </div>I understand but I would stick to more basic scenarios, if we get into the plot devices that the lore afford the whole thing might turn up insane for both sides.<br /> Otherwise we could also say that Voormas doesn't need to fight, he could just use a terrible Entropy 7 ritual to imprint the memetic idea of rebellion in the Dancers, so that they rebel and assassinate Zhyzhak, or even set on a curse with Entropy 6 that make sure that Zhyzhak will die in a few months, or again Voormas could curse the entire hive to extinction within few decades with Entropy 7 or make it crumble with Entropy 6.<br /> <br /> So I'd keep ourselves in the realms of normal devices, because in the realm of plot devices the whole thing would be resolved by a Fiat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everything you just said applies to Voormas as well. Mind you, even unstated characters should be able to be killed. I don't think any character should get Plot Armor. </div> </div> </div>Sure, besides it is the whole point of the main scenario of Ascension: kill Voormas<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the penalties are stacking up, which is going to make any magick used less effective overall.<br /> Oh, in this scenario, you also need to set an effect aside to enter/survive the Hive, it being a radioactive pit and all. That's yet another minor thing to keep track of. </div> </div> </div>In fact I said that the best thing would be prepare yourself before so that you don't need to cast later, and this is a general rule for Mage as a setting, not just for this scenario.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After the conversation so far, going way back to what started it, I do think if Voormas attacked the Trinity Caern Hive instead of some random minor pit there is a very good chance he would be killed. It'd be an interesting fight, but that is the wrong Hive to pick for an invasion. And overall, even though Voormas has stats, as does the Hive's most prominent member (Zhyzhak) this would still fall entirely in the realm of ST fiat. There's just too much that would be thrown around to have it be anything else. And unlike Zhyzhak, Voormas would stand out as a hell of a target for Spirals to throw themselves at. Zhyzhak would just be one Garou in a wall of fur and teeth/claws and so targeting her would be much less likely (not that he would know to). The forces they can bring to the field are arguably equal (again in the realm of fiat) and so that's kind of a draw. It would come down to Voormas vs a Hive of fallen Garou. I don't think his stats and magick will overcome that disadvantage. </div> </div> </div>The hive...is not a problem if he has time to cast.<br /> <br /> You see, one of the non Plot devices power of the Entropy 7 archsphere is the cascade effect:which, I will quote &quot;Assume that Voormas can target any number of creatures in his line of sight with a single success and that he can create Effects that jump from one target to another)<br /> <br /> So if he cast Entropy 7,Life 4,Spirit 4 effect to make a Dancer turn into homid form this spell will work on anybody he sees, so if he has the entire Hive in front of him the entire Hive will return homid, if he cast a fireball the entire Hive will be hitten, and if he cast a blessing to his allies all his allies will be hit, so just for saying Voormas could transform all the weapons his allies are using in silver, with a single spell.<br /> He could use Corrispondence 4 to cast the effect from very far, from a safe position.<br /> <br /> <br /> It would be not easy, it would be (in the case of the homid reverse) a... six success at difficulty 8 roll (Entropy 7+4, -3 spending 3 quintessence points,Five success to transform one and one extra success to hit all in his sight), not simple, he would need a 2-3 turns to do it probably, but if his forces can hold on against the Hive and giving him time to cast he can do it (he could ask for help in the ritual to get things faster).<br /> With 5 assistant he could quickly get 20-30 success effect in place in brief time.<br /> <br /> Which is basically what he did when he assaulted Cerberus, he remained in the rear lines providing &quot;magical artillery&quot; as the Pretas hordes advanced to the frontline.<br /> <br /> <br /> So thing is, he must be dealt quickly, he can be beaten for sure, but you should point to the head of the snake immediatly, because if he starts providing &quot;magical artillery&quot; there is not much the hive can do.<br /> <br /> <br /> So it probably would work this way: Voormas would play defensive, unleashing hordes of pretas,akuma and lesser servants to keep the hive busy, while he, helped by the mages of the Consanguinity, targets the Hive with magical artillery, providing at the same time blessings and healings for his horde.<br /> <br /> At this point Zhyzhak should lead a strike team behind enemy lines to struck down Voormas and the artillery before the Hive crumbles.<br /> <br /> <br /> (mmmh...not a bad scenario, coul be nice for a one shot epic battle).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-12-2016, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:32:25-07:00","id":968144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry I made a mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It would still be difficult 5 or 6, for an effect that could need 3 success, with 9 dices, far from impossible, against countermagic at difficulty 9.<br /> <br /> As for Friction Curse the system has never been given in detail<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Turning a subject's motion into heat energy, the mage not only renders the subject unable to move, but causes the victim to heat up until he bursts into flame! This Effect essentially turns the subject's movement into damage, so faster objects are more susceptible. A modified version can cause the subject's own breathing action to create cold, freezing the subject in place and encasing him in a block of ice. Partial successes negate some motion and impart some heat; multiple successes can transform motion into damage. Better still, since the target can't move, he is hard-pressed to dodge the ensuing eruption of fire or cold.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically it stops you, and if somehow you keep moving you are gonna suffer fire damage, the faster you are the more dire the consequences.<br /> <br /> Still since is not clear the master must establishing the working of it.<br /> If it was me, I'd say that you take 1 agg level of damage for every action you do, which means that a vampire with high levels of celerity could burst into flames if he use it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah probably when it comes to allies and forces they will fight on equal terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah maybe it so, but it's really not difficult to understand if your foe is werecreature, every mage with Mind 1 or Spirit 1 will be able to scan an aura.<br /> So it's very unlikely that something like that could happen, maybe with a very young mage who lacks even a dot in mind or spirit, but for sure is not something that is gonna happening to an experienced mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah but they say &quot;at least&quot;, so again if a game master would present you a Voormas with 6 or 8 dices it would be not strange at all, and it would be justified by the rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I understand but I would stick to more basic scenarios, if we get into the plot devices that the lore afford the whole thing might turn up insane for both sides.<br /> Otherwise we could also say that Voormas doesn't need to fight, he could just use a terrible Entropy 7 ritual to imprint the memetic idea of rebellion in the Dancers, so that they rebel and assassinate Zhyzhak, or even set on a curse with Entropy 6 that make sure that Zhyzhak will die in a few months, or again Voormas could curse the entire hive to extinction within few decades with Entropy 7 or make it crumble with Entropy 6.<br /> <br /> So I'd keep ourselves in the realms of normal devices, because in the realm of plot devices the whole thing would be resolved by a Fiat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, besides it is the whole point of the main scenario of Ascension: kill Voormas<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In fact I said that the best thing would be prepare yourself before so that you don't need to cast later, and this is a general rule for Mage as a setting, not just for this scenario.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The hive...is not a problem if he has time to cast.<br /> <br /> You see, one of the non Plot devices power of the Entropy 7 archsphere is the cascade effect:which, I will quote &quot;Assume that Voormas can target any number of creatures in his line of sight with a single success and that he can create Effects that jump from one target to another)<br /> <br /> So if he cast Entropy 7,Life 4,Spirit 4 effect to make a Dancer turn into homid form this spell will work on anybody he sees, so if he has the entire Hive in front of him the entire Hive will return homid, if he cast a fireball the entire Hive will be hitten, and if he cast a blessing to his allies all his allies will be hit, so just for saying Voormas could transform all the weapons his allies are using in silver, with a single spell.<br /> He could use Corrispondence 4 to cast the effect from very far, from a safe position.<br /> <br /> <br /> It would be not easy, it would be (in the case of the homid reverse) a... six success at difficulty 8 roll (Entropy 7+4, -3 spending 3 quintessence points,Five success to transform one and one extra success to hit all in his sight), not simple, he would need a 2-3 turns to do it probably, but if his forces can hold on against the Hive and giving him time to cast he can do it (he could ask for help in the ritual to get things faster).<br /> With 5 assistant he could quickly get 20-30 success effect in place in brief time.<br /> <br /> Which is basically what he did when he assaulted Cerberus, he remained in the rear lines providing &quot;magical artillery&quot; as the Pretas hordes advanced to the frontline.<br /> <br /> <br /> So thing is, he must be dealt quickly, he can be beaten for sure, but you should point to the head of the snake immediatly, because if he starts providing &quot;magical artillery&quot; there is not much the hive can do.<br /> <br /> <br /> So it probably would work this way: Voormas would play defensive, unleashing hordes of pretas,akuma and lesser servants to keep the hive busy, while he, helped by the mages of the Consanguinity, targets the Hive with magical artillery, providing at the same time blessings and healings for his horde.<br /> <br /> At this point Zhyzhak should lead a strike team behind enemy lines to struck down Voormas and the artillery before the Hive crumbles.<br /> <br /> <br /> (mmmh...not a bad scenario, coul be nice for a one shot epic battle).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's doubtful that even he could get those successes. Rolling to affect the hive in this context, because they're by and large maddened zealots for it that would ride it right up to the end, means overcoming the organisms hosting it, Grammaw, which is a miles-long thunderwyrm, which is also backed up by the Green Dragon as the caern totem. Which exists without the need for any magical support in a world that would not believe in it even while on an acid trip, and itself basically commands an entire system of spirits, some willing and many not. Good luck trying to swing past that metaphysical weight on a tactical time scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:43:33-07:00","id":968152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968144#post968144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's doubtful that even he could get those successes. Rolling to affect the hive in this context, because they're by and large maddened zealots for it that would ride it right up to the end, means overcoming the organisms hosting it, Grammaw, which is a miles-long thunderwyrm, which is also backed up by the Green Dragon as the caern totem. Which exists without the need for any magical support in a world that would not believe in it even while on an acid trip, and itself basically commands an entire system of spirits, some willing and many not. Good luck trying to swing past that metaphysical weight on a tactical time scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I really did not understand the whole matter with the Hive,could you explain it better?<br /> As for the spirits I don't see the problem really, he could kill the all the spirits with a Force 5,Matter 3,Spirit 5, Prime 2 effect, causing a spiritual nuclear explosion like the one in Bangladesh.<br /> It would be a...30 success effect,difficult 6 or 7 by spending quintessence,with help in the casting from the other mages it would be a 5-6 turn casting with lesser mages as help,and 3-4 with competent mages aiding the ritual (he commands several Liches, so I think they should manage it).<br /> It's the same as before, if they can't reach him in time there are few things he can't destroy, and with Correspondence 4 he can throw a lot of effects from pretty far, and if he doesn't have to be on the frontline probably he will not even need the prepared effects, he could just focus on setting on impenetrable defenses and long range attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously the first thing he should do in this scenario if he's really gonna play defensive is setting a 50 success ban Correspondence 4,Spirit 4,Prime 2 all around the &quot;magical artillery&quot; post to keep the spirits out; at a reduced difficulty of 5 is pretty much easy if other mages are helping you, and by sacrificing his pretas and using a Prime 3 effect (lambs of the slaughter) he can get a lot of quintessence to invest in the whole task.<br /> Even more he could put it from the distance devolving a few success more on it (like, from tokyo with 6 success more) and then teleporting there only after the stage is prepared.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT.<br /> <br /> Oh god he could even bring his gigantic living fortress as base for the artillery strikes, the castle walls are harder than modern tank armor, it walks on two legs and stomps everything on a 30 feet diameter (20 bashing <u>levels</u> x hit), he should just set the spirit ban on the castle and then advance or retreat as much as he needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-12-2016, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:44:37-07:00","id":968200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for Friction Curse the system has never been given in detail<br /> <br /> &quot;Turning a subject's motion into heat energy, the mage not only renders the subject unable to move, but causes the victim to heat up until he bursts into flame! This Effect essentially turns the subject's movement into damage, so faster objects are more susceptible. A modified version can cause the subject's own breathing action to create cold, freezing the subject in place and encasing him in a block of ice. Partial successes negate some motion and impart some heat; multiple successes can transform motion into damage. Better still, since the target can't move, he is hard-pressed to dodge the ensuing eruption of fire or cold.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically it stops you, and if somehow you keep moving you are gonna suffer fire damage, the faster you are the more dire the consequences.<br /> <br /> Still since is not clear the master must establishing the working of it.<br /> If it was me, I'd say that you take 1 agg level of damage for every action you do, which means that a vampire with high levels of celerity could burst into flames if he use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 Agg is really minor damage. It is more than a bit annoying that there is zero system written for it, but it continually gets brought up in crossover &quot;fights&quot; as then end all/be all for dealing with extra actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah maybe it so, but it's really not difficult to understand if your foe is werecreature, every mage with Mind 1 or Spirit 1 will be able to scan an aura.<br /> So it's very unlikely that something like that could happen, maybe with a very young mage who lacks even a dot in mind or spirit, but for sure is not something that is gonna happening to an experienced mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumes the Mage casts a sensing effect in advance. And if a Mage has never encountered a creature before, they very well could end up using the wrong Spheres to affect it. It isn't wholly unreasonable for a Mage to use Life/Matter to attack a Risen, thinking it a Vampire. Though this thought tangent doesn't directly apply here I do think it's a possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah but they say &quot;at least&quot;, so again if a game master would present you a Voormas with 6 or 8 dices it would be not strange at all, and it would be justified by the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, though I would guess that is so you can increase the difficulty of the fight to suit your game needs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I understand but I would stick to more basic scenarios, if we get into the plot devices that the lore afford the whole thing might turn up insane for both sides.<br /> Otherwise we could also say that Voormas doesn't need to fight, he could just use a terrible Entropy 7 ritual to imprint the memetic idea of rebellion in the Dancers, so that they rebel and assassinate Zhyzhak, or even set on a curse with Entropy 6 that make sure that Zhyzhak will die in a few months, or again Voormas could curse the entire hive to extinction within few decades with Entropy 7 or make it crumble with Entropy 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Werewolf side, most of that would flat out fail. Entropy 7 point, the Dancers would rebel and get put in their place. Entropy 6 point, Green Dragon would intervene (completely with an Incarna's power). On the entire hive extinction, several things stop that: Incarna intervention (pack totems, the caern totem, the very living Thunderwyrm Grandma) and the Hive's collective countermagic would make that not work I would think. And you can't make it crumble for the same reasons. Pretty much any spell that would auto-win the situation will automatically fail (imo) for various reasons. There is no easy insta-win scenario. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So I'd keep ourselves in the realms of normal devices, because in the realm of plot devices the whole thing would be resolved by a Fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure, besides it is the whole point of the main scenario of Ascension: kill Voormas</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: applies to Zhyzhak, albeit to a lesser degree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In fact I said that the best thing would be prepare yourself before so that you don't need to cast later, and this is a general rule for Mage as a setting, not just for this scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, and agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hive...is not a problem if he has time to cast.<br /> <br /> You see, one of the non Plot devices power of the Entropy 7 archsphere is the cascade effect:which, I will quote &quot;Assume that Voormas can target any number of creatures in his line of sight with a single success and that he can create Effects that jump from one target to another)<br /> So if he cast Entropy 7,Life 4,Spirit 4 effect to make a Dancer turn into homid form this spell will work on anybody he sees, so if he has the entire Hive in front of him the entire Hive will return homid, if he cast a fireball the entire Hive will be hitten, and if he cast a blessing to his allies all his allies will be hit, so just for saying Voormas could transform all the weapons his allies are using in silver, with a single spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I would say all abilities of Spheres above level 5 are arguably Plot Device powers, but that's neither here nor there. Going that route actually seems counter productive since that then incurs multiple countermagic rolls (targeting the Hive), which get added together to oppose the magic. I don't think he could actually pull that off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> He could use Corrispondence 4 to cast the effect from very far, from a safe position.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. This point was brought up earlier in the thread and I disagreed then. Caerns/Hives have a number of defenses. Targeting into them is actually not an easy task since they have scrying shields. Even assuming you can, especially in this case, you are casting magic <i>into</i> <u>both</u> a titanic creature which will have its own defenses and into the Caern Spirit which will also oppose it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would be not easy, it would be (in the case of the homid reverse) a... six success at difficulty 8 roll (Entropy 7+4, -3 spending 3 quintessence points,Five success to transform one and one extra success to hit all in his sight),</div> </div> </div> </div>+ the dif increase for ongoing effects.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not simple, he would need a 2-3 turns to do it probably, but if his forces can hold on against the Hive and giving him time to cast he can do it (he could ask for help in the ritual to get things faster).<br /> With 5 assistant he could quickly get 20-30 success effect in place in brief time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming he can see the Caern's defenders. The Caern is locating inside the guts of a several hundred foot long (conservatively) ThunderWyrm which is also mobile and can travel through the Earth, through pretty much any substance it could conceivably encounter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968101#post968101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which is basically what he did when he assaulted Cerberus, he remained in the rear lines providing &quot;magical artillery&quot; as the Pretas hordes advanced to the frontline.<br /> <br /> So thing is, he must be dealt quickly, he can be beaten for sure, but you should point to the head of the snake immediatly, because if he starts providing &quot;magical artillery&quot; there is not much the hive can do.<br /> <br /> So it probably would work this way: Voormas would play defensive, unleashing hordes of pretas,akuma and lesser servants to keep the hive busy, while he, helped by the mages of the Consanguinity, targets the Hive with magical artillery, providing at the same time blessings and healings for his horde.<br /> <br /> At this point Zhyzhak should lead a strike team behind enemy lines to struck down Voormas and the artillery before the Hive crumbles.<br /> <br /> <br /> (mmmh...not a bad scenario, coul be nice for a one shot epic battle).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree this would be an interesting scenario. There are a lot of factors that warp this from being anywhere near a straight forward fight. Most of the tactics Voormas would have used against Cerberus (admittedly, I'm not familiar with the fight) shouldn't work here. This isn't a simple fight against Spirals. The fact that the Caern is alive in both a material and spiritual sense really complicates matters. The Hive can literally just leave if need be. And throwing (what's a preta?) those minor minions isn't going to keep the hive terribly busy. They are going to be killed offhandedly (possibly by the Caern itself), and if things begin to go south the Hive will leave, all the while moon bridging in possibly hundreds more Garou.<br /> And there are plenty of answers to Voormas sitting in the back. Toss a few Nexus Crawlers. The high rank Theurges can levy all sorts of magic back. Garou aren't purely physical combat machines, though they certainly excel at that. You could have literal clouds of banes to deal with, reality warping left and right. Sitting at the back of an army doesn't help as much here I wouldn't think. The fortress that's being assaulted is mobile. In any case, it should obviously be able to be done. But I still think this would just end up failing.<br /> <br /> Funnier image is Voormas amassing his army and beginning the assault and just getting belly flopped by hundreds of tons of Grandmaw. Fight over. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:55:35-07:00","id":968208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968152#post968152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously the first thing he should do in this scenario if he's really gonna play defensive is setting a 50 success ban Correspondence 4,Spirit 4,Prime 2 all around the &quot;magical artillery&quot; post to keep the spirits out; at a reduced difficulty of 5 is pretty much easy if other mages are helping you, and by sacrificing his pretas and using a Prime 3 effect (lambs of the slaughter) he can get a lot of quintessence to invest in the whole task.<br /> Even more he could put it from the distance devolving a few success more on it (like, from tokyo with 6 success more) and then teleporting there only after the stage is prepared.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that ban keep out Spirit charms as well? otherwise Warp Reality is going to ruin their day. Also, exploding formori and Balefire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968152#post968152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh god he could even bring his gigantic living fortress as base for the artillery strikes, the castle walls are harder than modern tank armor, it walks on two legs and stomps everything on a 30 feet diameter (20 bashing <u>levels</u> x hit), he should just set the spirit ban on the castle and then advance or retreat as much as he needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually laughably weak compared to Grandmaw. He would advance once and never again.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:50:25-07:00","id":968248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968200#post968200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This assumes the Mage casts a sensing effect in advance. And if a Mage has never encountered a creature before, they very well could end up using the wrong Spheres to affect it. It isn't wholly unreasonable for a Mage to use Life/Matter to attack a Risen, thinking it a Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ture, I suppose that in a similar case the effect would simply fail to deliver.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fair point, though I would guess that is so you can increase the difficulty of the fight to suit your game needs. </div> </div> </div>Yeah but I don't think it would be very fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From the Werewolf side, most of that would flat out fail. Entropy 7 point, the Dancers would rebel and get put in their place. Entropy 6 point, Green Dragon would intervene (completely with an Incarna's power). On the entire hive extinction, several things stop that: Incarna intervention (pack totems, the caern totem, the very living Thunderwyrm Grandma) and the Hive's collective countermagic would make that not work I would think. And you can't make it crumble for the same reasons. Pretty much any spell that would auto-win the situation will automatically fail (imo) for various reasons. There is no easy insta-win scenario. </div> </div> </div>Agreed, besides as I said I'd prefer keeping this kinda of plot devices out from the scenario, it would reduce everything to a FIAT.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, I would say all abilities of Spheres above level 5 are arguably Plot Device powers, but that's neither here nor there. Going that route actually seems counter productive since that then incurs multiple countermagic rolls (targeting the Hive), which get added together to oppose the magic. I don't think he could actually pull that off. </div> </div> </div>I'm not completely sure that the countermagic works the same way with the cascade effect.<br /> <br /> You see you are not targeting an area, you are targeting multiple targets, that's the point of Entropy 7.<br /> <br /> So I think that the countermagic roll would be individual,they would not sum up, because is like if you are casting this effect on each one of them individually.<br /> <br /> Let's make an example, if I'd cast a 20 success ritual on an area, assuring that everyone in that area can't shapeshift their countermagic dices will sum up, so I will have to subract the total ammount of their success from my 20 success.<br /> If I'm casting the effect on two fera, with a 6 success roll (5 for the base effect and 1 for the extra target) I think the roll should be individual, so each one roll, let's say one get enough success to counter me, he doesn't turn, he is unaffected by my rote, but if the other one fails he is affected by it, so we will have one that countered and one that didn't.<br /> Otherwise it would make no sense the whole &quot;Targets: One additional target for each success beyond the Base.&quot; in the dividing success rule, because each times you use it on more than one target their summed up countermagic would blow you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think that the cascade effect reproduce the second scenario, because it's the whole thing that would make it special, any mage can cast a rote on an entire area, but only archmage with entropy 7 can do it like if it was an individual spell (the same phrasing of the effect suggest this, it says it's one effect that &quot;jumps&quot; from one target to another).<br /> <br /> So each Dancers should do his own counter roll,without summing up with the others.<br /> This means the best would counter it, while the younglings would succumb to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. This point was brought up earlier in the thread and I disagreed then. Caerns/Hives have a number of defenses. Targeting into them is actually not an easy task since they have scrying shields. Even assuming you can, especially in this case, you are casting magic <i>into</i> <u>both</u> a titanic creature which will have its own defenses and into the Caern Spirit which will also oppose it. </div> </div> </div>A good mage can unwave the shields, he just needs to rolls more success than the one requested to put up the shield.<br /> Given enough time there is not much a mage cannot unwave, exspecially if he is aided and remember that Voormas has the direct aid of 13 mages and a bunch of liches, if they all cooperate to pull down the shield there is not much that can resist.<br /> (let's even assume that each one of the Consaguinity has only arete 3, it would still be 48 dices to unwave the shields (3*13+ the 9 of Voormas)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> + the dif increase for ongoing effects. </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming that in the &quot;defensive strategy&quot; scenario Voormas do not have prepared effects, it would be unwise, he can let the mobs fight in the fronlines while he help them from the rear and focusing just on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> Assuming he can see the Caern's defenders. The Caern is locating inside the guts of a several hundred foot long (conservatively) ThunderWyrm which is also mobile and can travel through the Earth, through pretty much any substance it could conceivably encounter. </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree this would be an interesting scenario. There are a lot of factors that warp this from being anywhere near a straight forward fight. Most of the tactics Voormas would have used against Cerberus (admittedly, I'm not familiar with the fight) shouldn't work here. This isn't a simple fight against Spirals. The fact that the Caern is alive in both a material and spiritual sense really complicates matters. The Hive can literally just leave if need be.[QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, common Thunderwyrms are not that powerful.<br /> <br /> <br /> From the Book of the wyrm, W20<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attributes: Strength 8, Dexterity 4, Stamina 8, Charisma 0,<br /> <br /> Manipulation 0, Appearance 0, Perception 3, Intelligence<br /> 1, Wits 2<br /> <br /> Note: The Attributes listed above reflect the statistics for an average (30-foot) Thunderwyrm. Strength and Stamina increase substantially the larger they grow, and there appears to be no upper limit on how much they can grow. Grandmother Thunderwyrm is allegedly strong enough to shatter concrete by rippling her skin.<br /> <br /> Abilities: Athletics 5 (cannot dodge), Brawl 5<br /> <br /> Rage 6, Willpower 5<br /> <br /> <br /> Health Levels: OK, OK, OK, \u20131, \u20131, \u20131, \u20132, \u20132, \u20132, \u20133,<br /> \u20133, \u20134, \u20134, \u20135, \u20135, Incapacitated<br /> <br /> Attacks: Bite (Strength lethal), Roll (Strength bashing \u2014 more than 3 successes indicates the target is pinned under the creature\u2019s bulk), Body Slam (Strength + 3 bashing)<br /> Powers: Armor (four extra soak dice), Burrow (as the Garou Gift, but with no cost)<br /> <br /> Image: Thunderwyrms range in size from merely huge to unspeakably gigantic. The most commonly encountered normally stretch 30 feet in length, and almost eight feet wide. The largest, and presumably oldest, is Grandmother Thunderwyrm: she spans the length of two football fields and is almost three hundred feet around.<br /> Rumor has it that she contains an entire Wyrm caern in her gut. The smallest Thunderwyrm yet seen \u2014 presumably newly hatched \u2014 was only the length of a man.These pillars of pale grey flesh constantly secrete a thick, mucus-like substance to speed their way through the earth. They move through muscular contractions, and by eating everything ahead of them and defecating<br /> the earth out as they pass, leaving little trace of their presence. Thunderwyrms resemble earthworms with enormous mouths filled with row upon row of jagged teeth. Some are aquatic and develop rubbery black hides more like a leech. </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically the common Thunderwyrm is much weaker than the common Vozdh.<br /> <br /> And, even more importantly, it just has 2 dice of counter magic, which is...really not a lot.<br /> <br /> Now Grandmother Thunderwyrm is much times bigger, 240 yards, and it will have a much higher strenght* and stamina (but not dexterity).<br /> <br /> This means that Grandmother is gonna be slow (dexterity 4), even slower than Voormas (dexterity 6)<br /> <br /> At this point best thing would be targeting Grandmother Thunderwyrm, since she cannot escape, and since she will have a low countermagick dicepool (wits do not increase with size, so even Grandmother will have just 2 dice of countermagic) she can escape sure, but she will be slow.<br /> <br /> So since her countermagic is low there is plenty of tricks Voormas might play.<br /> (if her willpower is not gonna be higher than 5 there are plenty of dirty tricks a mage with Mind 4 can pull out from the hat)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But I think that if he wishes to end it fast and brutally a Force 5,Matter 3, Spirit 5, Prime 2 Spirit Nuke should kill it in one shot, no countermagic roll involved, and all that is spiritic inside him dying.<br /> <br /> It would be a...30-40 success ritual,with the help of his fellows mages he could pull it in 4-6 turns, with a bit of luck even less.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *But I don't even know how much, the description says Grandmother can shatter concrete by rippling her skin, well, any creature with Strenght 9 can punch through a cement wall without a roll, so I don't expect her strenght to be higher than 20.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And throwing (what's a preta?) those minor minions isn't going to keep the hive terribly busy. They are going to be killed offhandedly (possibly by the Caern itself), and if things begin to go south the Hive will leave, all the while moon bridging in possibly hundreds more Garou. </div> </div> </div>Beware, he doesn't have just a handful of pretas, he has thousands of them.<br /> (they are powerful hobgoblin that have been born from Voormas jhor, the weakest are pups with 4 health levels the strongest are tough guys with 10 healt levels).<br /> <br /> Plus the wraiths and akumas from the Hell of being skinned alive, and there are a lot of wraiths and akumas in the Hell of being skinned alive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And there are plenty of answers to Voormas sitting in the back. Toss a few Nexus Crawlers. The high rank Theurges can levy all sorts of magic back. Garou aren't purely physical combat machines, though they certainly excel at that. You could have literal clouds of banes to deal with, reality warping left and right. Sitting at the back of an army doesn't help as much here I wouldn't think. The fortress that's being assaulted is mobile. In any case, it should obviously be able to be done. But I still think this would just end up failing. </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said best thing would be prepare a powerful ban, casting it from the distance with Correspondence 4 and putting himself in the battle just after that.<br /> This way Nexus Crawler and banes would be blocked by the Ban.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Funnier image is Voormas amassing his army and beginning the assault and just getting belly flopped by hundreds of tons of Grandmaw. Fight over. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> </div> </div> </div>Well that's unlikely, in case of trouble he could just teleport himself in Honk Kong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-12-2016, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:09:03-07:00","id":968307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, besides as I said I'd prefer keeping this kinda of plot devices out from the scenario, it would reduce everything to a FIAT.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what any of those effects are though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not completely sure that the countermagic works the same way with the cascade effect.<br /> <br /> You see you are not targeting an area, you are targeting multiple targets, that's the point of Entropy 7.<br /> <br /> So I think that the countermagic roll would be individual,they would not sum up, because is like if you are casting this effect on each one of them individually.<br /> <br /> Let's make an example, if I'd cast a 20 success ritual on an area, assuring that everyone in that area can't shapeshift their countermagic dices will sum up, so I will have to subract the total ammount of their success from my 20 success.<br /> If I'm casting the effect on two fera, with a 6 success roll (5 for the base effect and 1 for the extra target) I think the roll should be individual, so each one roll, let's say one get enough success to counter me, he doesn't turn, he is unaffected by my rote, but if the other one fails he is affected by it, so we will have one that countered and one that didn't.<br /> Otherwise it would make no sense the whole &quot;Targets: One additional target for each success beyond the Base.&quot; in the dividing success rule, because each times you use it on more than one target their summed up countermagic would blow you.<br /> <br /> I think that the cascade effect reproduce the second scenario, because it's the whole thing that would make it special, any mage can cast a rote on an entire area, but only archmage with entropy 7 can do it like if it was an individual spell (the same phrasing of the effect suggest this, it says it's one effect that &quot;jumps&quot; from one target to another).<br /> <br /> So each Dancers should do his own counter roll,without summing up with the others.<br /> This means the best would counter it, while the younglings would succumb to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And prior to M20 Nightfolk didn't get innate countermagic. I chalk it up to new rules not playing nice with the old ones. Before, you had to allocate successes to add targets. That was the bonus of the Cascade effect. It included all of line of sight in 1 successes instead of needing however many targets you could see in the successes. I can see why you want to err on the side of increasing it's power, but I do think it is already very powerful. You just have to choose your targets wisely. A Caern/Hive of Garou is not the prime target for that effect, imo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good mage can unwave the shields, he just needs to rolls more success than the one requested to put up the shield.<br /> Given enough time there is not much a mage cannot unwave, exspecially if he is aided and remember that Voormas has the direct aid of 13 mages and a bunch of liches, if they all cooperate to pull down the shield there is not much that can resist.<br /> (let's even assume that each one of the Consaguinity has only arete 3, it would still be 48 dices to unwave the shields (3*13+ the 9 of Voormas)</div> </div> </div> </div>a few things. I agree the defenses can be unweaved. It will take time though, and in this case it's taking the attention of the big bad and his aids. They also need to overcome more than the successes to set up the defenses I would think. Since rites involved are tied directly into the Caern. At that point you are going up against the Caern Incarna.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm assuming that in the &quot;defensive strategy&quot; scenario Voormas do not have prepared effects, it would be unwise, he can let the mobs fight in the fronlines while he help them from the rear and focusing just on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now, common Thunderwyrms are not that powerful<br /> <br /> Basically the common Thunderwyrm is much weaker than the common Vozdh.<br /> <br /> And, even more importantly, it just has 2 dice of counter magic, which is...really not a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you have no idea what their countermagic is because they are never statted out for fighting Mages (it's almost like Thunderwyrms don't exist in the world of Mage. Weird, I know). The same creatures in both lines have different (relevant) stats in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now Grandmother Thunderwyrm is much times bigger, 240 yards, and it will have a much higher strenght* and stamina (but not dexterity).<br /> <br /> This means that Grandmother is gonna be slow (dexterity 4), even slower than Voormas (dexterity 6)</div> </div> </div> </div>Dex is only slightly related to speed, as a modifier. Grandmaw's base speed is going to be much much higher, because it/she is much much bigger. That's just kind of how it is going to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At this point best thing would be targeting Grandmother Thunderwyrm, since she cannot escape, and since she will have a low countermagick dicepool (wits do not increase with size, so even Grandmother will have just 2 dice of countermagic) she can escape sure, but she will be slow.<br /> <br /> So since her countermagic is low there is plenty of tricks Voormas might play.<br /> (if her willpower is not gonna be higher than 5 there are plenty of dirty tricks a mage with Mind 4 can pull out from the hat)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to assume from the tone of your part of the conversation throughout that this isn't a joke or trolling. Average Thunderwyrms have the stats you quoted. Wits may not increase with Size. Wits definitely should increase with Age/Experience. Same with Willpower (which should be 10+) and every other applicable stat. You seem to think that Voormas would be able to outrun Grandmaw? A Wyrm over 700 feet long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But I think that if he wishes to end it fast and brutally a Force 5,Matter 3, Spirit 5, Prime 2 Spirit Nuke should kill it in one shot, no countermagic roll involved, and all that is spiritic inside him dying.<br /> <br /> It would be a...30-40 success ritual,with the help of his fellows mages he could pull it in 4-6 turns, with a bit of luck even less.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you either vastly overestimate the Nuke, or more likely underestimate Grandmaw. ThunderWyrms are born from Nukes. I wouldn't be surprised if it did absolutely nothing to it. And how many turns are you designating now to various things. The Spirals do actually have mystics capable of countering effects. And at this point, you have several turns worth of setting up a ban (that wards Spirits, but that Grandmaw is going to roll over) and now another several turns to summon a Nuke, that may or may not do what you want it to. You also portray the ability to do such a feat as something relatively simple, which I'm going to assume actually takes a lot more work than portrayed, or else it would happen a lot more often in game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But I don't even know how much, the description says Grandmother can shatter concrete by rippling her skin, well, any creature with Strenght 9 can punch through a cement wall without a roll, so I don't expect her strenght to be higher than 20.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Zmei at 40 feet or so have Strengths around 18-20. Grandmaw is way way higher than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Beware, he doesn't have just a handful of pretas, he has thousands of them.<br /> (they are powerful hobgoblin that have been born from Voormas jhor, the weakest are pups with 4 health levels the strongest are tough guys with 10 healt levels).</div> </div> </div> </div>So equivalent to a combat fomori. They are going to die swarming down Grandmaw's gullet, or in her digestive juices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Plus the wraiths and akumas from the Hell of being skinned alive, and there are a lot of wraiths and akumas in the Hell of being skinned alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraiths are treated as Spirits from the Werewolf side of it, so those aren't going to be terribly helpful. There are more than enough Gifts that work on spirits that I'm going to disregard them altogether. Akumas could be a factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As I said best thing would be prepare a powerful ban, casting it from the distance with Correspondence 4 and putting himself in the battle just after that.<br /> This way Nexus Crawler and banes would be blocked by the Ban.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ban should have to have some sort of actual setup. That setup is going to be vulnerable to Warp Reality. Honestly, anything they do to defend against spirits is going to be vulnerable. A few uses of it (Warp Reality) and that ban is going to come crashing down. The way Spirits are set up, all Charms are not created equal, and some Charms are just better. Warp/Break Reality uses are going to need dedicated Mages to counter. If you don't counter the effects as their happening, you're kind of screwed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968248#post968248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's unlikely, in case of trouble he could just teleport himself in Honk Kong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I suppose running away is an option, but that makes this scenario much less interesting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T22:20:41-07:00","id":968372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bj7R_2WWdKs\" data-code=\"Bj7R_2WWdKs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Bj7R_2WWdKs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Edit: This one is more to the point, I think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 09-13-2016, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T22:49:49-07:00","id":968384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift?p=968307#post968307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to assume from the tone of your part of the conversation throughout that this isn't a joke or trolling. Average Thunderwyrms have the stats you quoted. Wits may not increase with Size. Wits definitely should increase with Age/Experience. Same with Willpower (which should be 10+) and every other applicable stat. You seem to think that Voormas would be able to outrun Grandmaw? A Wyrm over 700 feet long.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have some vague guidelines on the Gaian side with rorqual, but even the largest rorqual is likely several times smaller than Grammaw, and not as well-protected, or possessed of a superheated bone ram that can burn through most rock.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you either vastly overestimate the Nuke, or more likely underestimate Grandmaw. ThunderWyrms are born from Nukes. I wouldn't be surprised if it did absolutely nothing to it. And how many turns are you designating now to various things. The Spirals do actually have mystics capable of countering effects. And at this point, you have several turns worth of setting up a ban (that wards Spirits, but that Grandmaw is going to roll over) and now another several turns to summon a Nuke, that may or may not do what you want it to. You also portray the ability to do such a feat as something relatively simple, which I'm going to assume actually takes a lot more work than portrayed, or else it would happen a lot more often in game. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Grammaw likely has an immunity to bans, being a critter that's as much flesh as spirit. Also, as for the nuke... her blood is basically balefire (be careful not to pierce that hydrostatic skeleton!), and furmlings live in her body in massive amounts. You're just going to supercharge them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Zmei at 40 feet or so have Strengths around 18-20. Grandmaw is way way higher than that. </div> </div> </div>She has no stats... just a map. Stats would be less relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So equivalent to a combat fomori. They are going to die swarming down Grandmaw's gullet, or in her digestive juices. </div> </div> </div>A sizable number of them will get crapped out as ferectoi, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wraiths are treated as Spirits from the Werewolf side of it, so those aren't going to be terribly helpful. There are more than enough Gifts that work on spirits that I'm going to disregard them altogether. Akumas could be a factor. </div> </div> </div>Not usually, according to the ST Handbook, but ghosts are likely not going to be able to do much to the massive broodmother of all thunderwyrms. If any of them manage to get near the living spirit world, they're probably going to be in some serious trouble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well I suppose running away is an option, but that makes this scenario much less interesting.<br /> </div> </div> </div>It's the logical conclusion of Voormas actually seeing what's under the New Mexico desert in the WoD: not wanting to die, he nopes right the fuck back to the Hell of Being Skinned Alive, to attend and be entertained by its literal D&amp;D knockoff Yama Queen. Seriously, Tou Mu's description is straight out of Deities &amp; Demigods. I'll never stop harping on this, or the demon archer with the name that has syllables not in most Chinese languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T04:21:39-07:00","id":968448,"title":"","content":"A Warding ritual using the older WoD: Sorcerer book would protect from the gift by offering countermagic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T03:45:48-07:00","id":969125,"title":"","content":"(gotta lot of things to do in these days, I'll resume the topic later <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}